    "created_at": "2016-02-22T07:12:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-22T07:12:31Z",
    "body": "There's also a notion of [sequential focus navigation starting point](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#sequential-focus-navigation-starting-point) in the HTML spec, which Chromium does not implement (yet), and we get lots of non-compatibility reports.\nSee [crbug 454172](http://crbug.com/454172) and bugs that are merged to it.\n\nProbably we want to fix the fixup rule 1 such that when a focused node disappears, update the\n'sequential focus navigation starting point' to the node or its nearest ancestor (if it is removed from tree) to continue the tab order search from there.\n\nI'm happy to work on updating the spec :)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
